-{"id":"AUG-121","status":"in_progress","priority":"P1","complexity":4,"title":"[P1] Model each Auger task as a scoped XML spec with explicit in/out references and ch:trace links","reasoning":"Owner clarification 2026-10-30: a task is itself a small spec for one exact request, or it names the exact reusable spec blocks in scope and the relevant blocks explicitly out of scope. It must be searchable in one pass and preserve active/inactive, levels, verification, and provenance. Scope for THIS row: XML task element schema; stable task id matching the canonical board id; explicit in_scope refs, out_of_scope refs plus exclusion reason, acceptance/verification refs, status/version; approved-plan export using only supported boardctl fields; ch:trace spec IDs. Exclusions: do not change GitReins, scheduler dispatch, boardctl storage schema, or existing tasks 118/119/120; no direct JSONL writer, no LLM inference, no automatic task approval. Source: docs/prd/xml-spec-graph.md#requirements (R2,R3,R4,R9,R10) and #acceptance-criteria (AC-6,AC-7,AC-9,AC-15).\nch:trace row=AUG-121 spec=docs/prd/xml-spec-graph.md#requirements wave=none:task-not-dispatched test=none:not-implemented doc=docs/prd/xml-spec-graph.md prompt=none:not-dispatched evidence=none:not-run witness=none:proposal-only verdict=none:not-judged commit=none:not-implemented memory=/project/auger/prd/xml-spec-graph-2026-10-29","acceptance_criteria":"1. Given a task XML block, when validation runs, then its stable ID, lifecycle/version, in-scope refs, out-of-scope refs with reasons, acceptance refs, and verification methods are typed and resolve to existing blocks; proof: tests/test_xml_task_contract.py::test_task_scope_contract.\n2. Given duplicate, missing, inactive-without-acknowledgment, or cross-version spec references, when validation runs, then it returns a typed finding naming the exact task and block IDs without emitting a partial task packet; proof: the negative fixture cases in tests/test_xml_task_contract.py.\n3. Given an approved plan digest, when Auger exports one task through boardctl, then the canonical row records the exact in-scope and excluded block IDs plus their source version in existing supported fields and the read-back matches byte-for-byte; proof: an ephemeral boardctl fixture comparing the approved packet to boardctl show.\n4. Given an unapproved or stale plan digest, when task export is requested, then boardctl is not invoked and both canonical JSONL files remain byte-identical; proof: before/after hashes in tests/test_xml_task_contract.py.\n5. Given a task packet, when its trace marker is generated, then ch:trace row and spec fields resolve to the canonical task and exact XML IDs, while absent evidence/verdict/commit fields use none:<reason>; proof: a marker parser fixture and docs/prd/xml-spec-graph.md trace contract.\n6. Out of scope: no scheduler dispatch or task completion automation; proof: a test asserts the exporter invokes only boardctl create/readback and has no scheduler mutation client.","depends_on":["AUG-118","AUG-119"],"files_changed":[],"foreman_note":"PARTIAL - DO NOT REBUILD THE HALF THAT WORKS (measured 2026-11-05, HEAD 10ef0d7). EXISTS (landed ea819d9): attribute/ID selection machinery - select_spec_blocks (auger.py:8131), _spec_matches (:8116), forward closure SPEC_FORWARD_CLOSURE_ATTRS=('depends-on',) expanded by assembly, inverse closure ('verifies',) expanded from the verifying side, and every emitted block carries a file.xml#ID source citation. Proven live: 'spec assemble tests/fixtures/xml/specs --kind requirement --applies-to auger.export' -> 3 matched + 2 closure blocks, byte-identical across runs. MISSING: the task-scoped contract this row actually asks for - no task block type, no in-scope/out-of-scope attribute pair, no exclusion reasons, and the AC's named proof file tests/test_xml_task_contract.py does not exist. A worker should add the task-scope model on top of the working selector/closure layer, not re-implement selection.\n\nSG7 dispatch 2026-11-06 (goal auger-xml-hardening). Writer launched on /home/kara/proj-wt-auger-xml-hardening branch wt/auger-xml-hardening from base bb804d4; brief /home/kara/.hermes/goals/auger-xml-hardening-SG7-brief.txt. Scope: task-scoped XML block contract (AUG-121) + one-query minimal context bundle (AUG-122), built on the landed selection/closure primitive — do not rebuild select_spec_blocks/_spec_matches/assembly closure. Proof files tests/test_xml_task_contract.py and tests/test_spec_context.py are ABSENT at base (measured 2026-11-06) and neither is named in tests/gate.sh's pytest arm; the worker must create both, name both in the arm, and prove the arm assertion fails if they are dropped.\n\nSG7 LANDED, AWAITING VERDICT (driver tick 2026-11-06). Commits f4e79f0 (AUG-121 task contract) + 0df1c62 (AUG-122 context) on wt/auger-xml-hardening, ff-merged to main at 0df1c62. Driver re-ran the decisive arms itself: focused tests/test_xml_task_contract.py + tests/test_spec_context.py = 21 passed (evidence/sg7/01-focused.txt); worktree gate rc 0 (565 passed, 2 skipped, 887s); MERGED main gate rc 0 (565 passed, 2 skipped, 875s) with PATH=$PWD/.venv/bin:$PATH DUCKBRAIN_URL=http://127.0.0.1:3000 AUGER_GATE_PYTEST_BUDGET=3000s bash tests/gate.sh. Both new files are named in tests/gate.sh's pytest arm (19 files) and test_gate_arm_runs_these_files fails when either name is dropped (evidence/sg7/03-gate-arm.txt). Tests-first proof evidence/sg7/00-red.txt = 21 failed pre-implementation. No gitreins verdict run, so status stays in_progress.","worker_status":"done","commit_hash":null,"completed_at":null,"guard_result":null,"ci_result":null,"detail":{"fingerprint":"a4aa88b23c9f7ea1879723095f961401ead0f5fcd11f70d3e87ad4d5c47ed1a2"},"lines_added":0,"lines_removed":0,"attempts":0,"blocked_reason":null,"capability_tags":["xml","task-contract","scope","ch-trace","boardctl"],"created_at":"2026-10-30T05:56:07.352485+00:00","updated_at":"2026-11-06T14:19:53.245395+00:00","work