 {"id":"AUG-122","status":"in_progress","priority":"P1","complexity":4,"title":"[P1] Resolve a task or code location to a minimal XML spec context bundle in one query","reasoning":"Owner clarification 2026-10-30: when an agent reaches code it does not understand, it must use the same graph/query tool to find the spec related to that code instantly; one search returns only relevant blocks, not the irrelevant corpus. Scope for THIS row: a read-only Auger context query keyed by task ID, XML block ID/ch:trace spec reference, code path, or symbol; deterministic relationship expansion; include task scope and exclusion summary; report active/inactive state and verification. Exclusions: no full-corpus fallback, no code/spec edits, no arbitrary remote URL fetch, no second semantic/LLM backend, no GitReins hook wiring (GR-154). Source: docs/prd/xml-spec-graph.md#selection-and-assembly, #relationship-and-verification-graph, and #acceptance-criteria (AC-3,AC-4,AC-8,AC-9,AC-14).\nch:trace row=AUG-122 spec=docs/prd/xml-spec-graph.md#selection-and-assembly wave=none:task-not-dispatched test=none:not-implemented doc=docs/prd/xml-spec-graph.md prompt=none:not-dispatched evidence=none:not-run witness=none:proposal-only verdict=none:not-judged commit=none:not-implemented memory=/project/auger/prd/xml-spec-graph-2026-10-29","acceptance_criteria":"1. Given an Auger task ID, when the context query runs once, then it returns that task block, only its in-scope requirements/acceptance/verification blocks, and a compact explicit out-of-scope list with exclusion reasons; proof: tests/test_spec_context.py::test_task_context_excludes_unrelated_blocks.\n2. Given a source path or symbol with a ch:trace spec reference, when the context query runs, then it resolves the exact XML block and declared graph closure with source file, ID, version, active status, applicability, verification method, and relationship edge; proof: tests/test_spec_context.py::test_code_trace_context.\n3. Given no trace, an unknown symbol, an inactive block, or an ambiguous match, when the context query runs, then it returns an explicit structured unscoped/ambiguous/inactive result and never substitutes a whole-document or whole-corpus dump; proof: dedicated negative fixtures.\n4. Given the same query and XML tree, when run twice, then selected IDs, provenance order, and serialized output are byte-identical; proof: golden JSON fixture plus repeated digest equality.\n5. Given a corpus containing unrelated active blocks, when a narrow task/code query runs, then none of those unrelated blocks appear in the response and the response reports selected count, dependency count, input bytes, and output bytes; proof: decoy-block fixture and benchmark JSON.\n6. Out of scope: this query does not dispatch work, write boards, edit code, or call an LLM; proof: tests use a read-only fixture and assert no write/client seams are invoked.","depends_on":["AUG-118","AUG-121"],"files_changed":[],"foreman_note":"PARTIAL - DO NOT REBUILD THE HALF THAT WORKS (measured 2026-11-05, HEAD 10ef0d7). EXISTS (landed ea819d9): one-query resolution of a block by ID or selector plus its declared graph closure, with provenance. Proven live: 'spec list --id AUG-SHARED-DETERMINISM' -> shared.xml#AUG-SHARED-DETERMINISM (a block resolved out of a second file), and 'spec assemble' returns matched + closure blocks with source, version and status fields. MISSING: the task-scoped minimal context bundle - no in-scope/out-of-scope split with exclusion reasons, no ch:trace path/symbol resolution, and the AC's named proof file tests/test_spec_context.py does not exist. Build the task-context layer over the working selection primitive; the primitive itself is done and tested (tests/test_xml_specs.py::test_selects_only_requested_blocks_and_their_dependencies, ::test_no_deps_emits_only_the_matched_block, ::test_verifies_expands_from_the_requirement_not_from_the_criterion).\n\nSG7 dispatch 2026-11-06 (goal auger-xml-hardening). Writer launched on /home/kara/proj-wt-auger-xml-hardening branch wt/auger-xml-hardening from base bb804d4; brief /home/kara/.hermes/goals/auger-xml-hardening-SG7-brief.txt. Scope: task-scoped XML block contract (AUG-121) + one-query minimal context bundle (AUG-122), built on the landed selection/closure primitive — do not rebuild select_spec_blocks/_spec_matches/assembly closure. Proof files tests/test_xml_task_contract.py and tests/test_spec_context.py are ABSENT at base (measured 2026-11-06) and neither is named in tests/gate.sh's pytest arm; the worker must create both, name both in the arm, and prove the arm assertion fails if they are dropped.\n\nSG7 LANDED, AWAITING VERDICT (driver tick 2026-11-06). Commit 0df1c62 (chains f4e79f0) on wt/auger-xml-hardening, ff-merged to main at 0df1c62; driver-measured 21 focused tests green, worktree gate rc 0 and MERGED main gate rc 0 (565 passed / 2 skipped, 875s, transcript /home/kara/.hermes/goals/sg7-merged-gate.log). spec context landed: build_spec_context/render_spec_context/cmd_spec_context, in-scope/out-of-scope with exclusion reasons, ch:trace path+symbol resolution, byte-identical repeat output with measured input/output bytes, and a fixed-point counts.output_bytes. Falsifiers in evidence/sg7/04-falsifiers.txt (unknown symbol and no-trace answer status=unscoped with 0 decoys leaked, not a corpus dump; unapproved export leaves the board byte-identical). File named in tests/gate.sh's pytest arm with an arm-naming assertion that bites (evidence/sg7/03-gate-arm.txt). No gitreins verdict, status stays in_progress.","worker_status":"done","commit_hash":null,"completed_at":null,"guard_result":null,"ci_result":null,"detail":{"fingerprint":"a42454df3cb9ed3a01e2c0b9f8e880d2280c18b90bfea779cfe8fc17d4fe22f3"},"lines_added":0,"lines_removed":0,"attempts":0,"blocked_reason":null,"capability_tags":["xml","retrieval","graph","code-context","ch-trace"],"created_at":"2026-10-30T05:56:07.46538+00:00","updated_at":"2026-11-06T14:19:56.510828+00:00","worktree":"/home/kara/proj-wt-auger-xml-hardening","branch":"wt/auger-xml-hardening"}
 {"id":"AUG-123","status":"blocked","priority":"P1","complexity":4,"title":"[P1] Add first-class XML test and verification obligations, including migration-file coverage","reasoning":"Owner clarification 2026-10-30: specifications must say what tests are required, not merely name a verification method. A database migration requirement must pull in a test that applies the named migration file from the supported prior schema. Scope for THIS row: typed verification/test nodes linked to requirements; stable IDs, active/inactive lifecycle/version, target file or code surface, tracked test path/name, runner/selector metadata, fixture/precondition, expected assertions, and evidence form; query assembly returns only the selected requirements’ test obligations. XML references tracked tests; it never supplies arbitrary shell text for execution. Out of scope: changing production migration files, adding a new test runner, implementing GitReins handoff, or treating a package-suite pass as proof of a migration-specific test. Source: docs/prd/xml-spec-graph.md#R15 and #AC-17; depends on AUG-118 for the XML graph.\nch:trace row=AUG-123 spec=docs/prd/xml-spec-graph.md#R15 wave=none:task-not-dispatched test=none:not-implemented doc=docs/prd/xml-spec-graph.md prompt=none:not-dispatched evidence=none:not-run witness=none:proposal-only verdict=none:not-judged commit=none:not-implemented memory=/project/auger/xml-spec-task-tests-gitreins-2026-10-30","acceptance_criteria":"- **AC-17 (T):** Given a requirement linked to a database migration verification node, when Auger assembles the requirement, then the same bundle includes the exact migration path, supported prior-schema fixture, tracked test path/name, runner/selector metadata, expected schema/data assertions, and rollback test obligation when rollback is declared supported; proof: a fixture whose test actually applies the named migration file and fails when that file is replaced by a no-op.\nGiven duplicate, dangling, stale-version, or untracked test references, when schema validation runs, then it returns a typed failure naming the requirement and test IDs and emits no partial verification bundle; proof: `tests/test_verification_graph.py::test_invalid_test_refs_fail_closed`.\nGiven an XML test obligation, when Auger serializes it, then the runner/selector resolves only through the repository test harness and a tracked path/name; no raw XML shell command is executed; proof: `tests/test_verification_graph.py::test_xml_cannot_execute_arbitrary_shell`.\nGiven a migration fixture whose named migration file is replaced by a no-op, when its linked test runs from the supported prior schema, then the test fails on the expected schema/data assertions; proof: `tests/test_verification_graph.py::test_migration_obligation_applies_named_file`.\nOut of scope: this row adds schema/selection contracts only; it does not modify a production database migration or introduce a second test runner; proof: diff and test fixture contain only spec/test-contract files.","depends_on":["AUG-118"],"files_changed":[],"foreman_note":"SUBSTANTIALLY BUILT - BLOCKED ON A VERDICT, NOT ON CODE (measured 2026-11-05, HEAD 10ef0d7). Code is on origin/main as dae1769 (row commit_hash): SPEC_RUNNERS whitelist (auger.py:8405), obligation validation (auger.py:8473-8540: runner whitelist, git ls-files --error-unmatch tracked-file check, AST selector verification, migration + prior-schema fixture existence, non-empty assertions), and the typed test/verification path that AUG-128 later unblocked for method=\"test\". 40 tests pass including test_assembles_migration_obligation_with_repo_harness_metadata, test_rejects_duplicate_dangling_stale_and_unregistered_test_refs, test_serialized_runner_is_argument_vector_not_shell_command, and test_migration_obligation_applies_named_file_and_detects_noop. The apply/no-op clause was mutation-proven: replacing tests/fixtures/xml/verification/migrations/001_add_marker.sql with '-- no-op', and separately with a commented-out body, both turn the named test red; the file was restored and the tree is clean. ROW STAYS BLOCKED for the recorded reason: two judge verdicts FAIL, Tier 2 INCOMPLETE at the iteration cap, and the merged-tree full gate red on an unrelated live JEV test (test_feedback_live_proposes_gates_and_asks_a_real_question: jev_already_answered=-1) - not on this feature. Known residual (not a rebuild): rollback is unsupported with no machine-readable declaration in the schema. A worker re-implementing this row would duplicate ~150 lines of working, tested obligation checking.","worker_status":"pending","commit_hash":"dae176931177648fa5c8e9f2a71fea8f5404cb14","completed_at":null,"guard_result":"FAIL","ci_result":"GREEN","detail":{"fingerprint":"a081ca6904f0cf8bf9fbb3dfccd7c94510eeaae9738dc5bfc949d9335e0ec82e"},"lines_added":0,"lines_removed":0,"attempts":0,"blocked_reason":"Recovery fixup commit dae176931177648fa5c8e9f2a71fea8f5404cb14 is on origin/main and focused XML acceptance passed (33 passed), but the merged-tree full gate is red on unrelated live JEV assertion test_feedback_live_proposes_gates_and_asks_a_real_question: jev_already_answered=-1. GitReins async job job-13e87f5cb8464406aa619f89b8131bcf returned Tier 1 FAIL and Tier 2 INCOMPLETE at iteration cap; no passing merged-tree verdict exists.","capability_tags":["xml","verification","test-graph","migrations"],"created_at":"2026-10-30T06:17:57.180219+00:00","updated_at":"2026-11-05T12:59:25.512185+00:00","worker_summary":"Recovery fixup landed on main; row blocked by unrelated live JEV full-gate failure and non-passing GitReins verdict."}
 {"id":"AUG-124","status":"in_progress","priority":"P1","complexity":5,"title":"[P1] Package canonical boardctl tasks with scoped Auger specs and tests for GitReins judging","reasoning":"Owner clarification 2026-10-30: GitReins must receive the canonical task from boardctl together with exact spec scope and required test links, then judge from those sources rather than accepting this agent’s summary as truth. Scope for THIS row: read the exact canonical row through the supported boardctl read surface; resolve its spec/test refs through Auger; package board acceptance criteria verbatim, included/excluded block IDs with reasons, active/inactive state, source versions/digests, test refs/runner selectors, and a collision-safe board-ID mapping; validate ch:trace before any GitReins task/judge starts; read back the created GitReins task. Out of scope: direct JSONL writes, a second XML parser/evaluator, changing GitReins internals (GR-155), task dispatch/completion, or treating worker_summary/commit prose as evidence. Source: docs/prd/xml-spec-graph.md#R14, #R16, and #AC-16, #AC-18–AC-20. Depends on AUG-119, AUG-120, AUG-121, AUG-122, and AUG-123; GR-154 is the separately owned GitReins pre-commit task.\nch:trace row=AUG-124 spec=docs/prd/xml-spec-graph.md#R16 wave=none:task-not-dispatched test=none:not-implemented doc=docs/prd/xml-spec-graph.md prompt=none:not-dispatched evidence=none:not-run witness=none:proposal-only verdict=none:not-judged commit=none:not-implemented memory=/project/auger/xml-spec-task-tests-gitreins-2026-10-30","acceptance_criteria":"- **AC-16 (T):** Given a task packet containing in-scope and out-of-scope XML references across multiple files, active and inactive blocks, and unrelated decoys, when Auger assembles the task context, then it returns only the task, in-scope blocks and required graph closure, plus the explicit out-of-scope IDs/reasons; each returned block includes source ID, file, version, and status; proof: `tests/test_task_context.py::test_scope_and_exclusions_are_explicit`.\n- **AC-18 (T):** Given an approved boardctl task and its XML task/test references, when Auger creates the GitReins packet, then the packet preserves the board acceptance criteria verbatim, in/out-of-scope refs, exact test obligations, board ID or explicit ID mapping, and source digests; read-back equals the approved input and repeated export is idempotent; proof: an isolated boardctl/GitReins fixture with byte/digest comparison.\n- **AC-19 (T):** Given a missing, stale, ambiguous, or out-of-scope `ch:trace` reference, when the boardctl→GitReins handoff is requested, then no GitReins judge starts and the result names the invalid row/spec/test IDs; a valid trace starts the existing GitReins lifecycle with the same board acceptance criteria; proof: paired negative/positive integration tests asserting the judge invocation count.\n- **AC-20 (T):** Given a worker summary that claims a test passed while the required migration test is absent or fails on the committed tree, when GitReins evaluates the task packet, then the verdict is not PASS and cites the missing/failed test obligation; proof: a judge-context integration fixture with a deliberately false worker summary and a red migration test.","depends_on":["AUG-119","AUG-120","AUG-121","AUG-122","AUG-123"],"files_changed":[],"foreman_note":"ZERO CODE - GENUINELY UNSTARTED (measured 2026-11-05, HEAD 10ef0d7). 'grep -c boardctl auger.py' -> 0; no task-packet builder, no canonical board-row reader, no digest emitter, no read-back comparator, and AC-16's named proof file tests/test_task_context.py does not exist. The WIRE FORMAT is already defined on the consuming side: GitReins ships engine/auger_packet.py (TaskPacketAdapter) and engine/judge.py::_prepare_auger_task, which fails closed to Tier 1 on PacketValidationError. So the producer must match a real, existing consumer - a worker should read that adapter before designing the packet, and must not invent a second format. Nothing on the Auger side exists to extend.\n\nSG8 DISPATCHED 2026-11-06 from base 53f09d3 (goal auger-xml-hardening). Brief /home/kara/.hermes/goals/auger-xml-hardening-SG8-brief.txt. The CONSUMER is real and must be matched, not invented: /home/kara/gitreins/engine/auger_packet.py (TaskPacketAdapter._unresolved) + engine/judge.py::_prepare_auger_task fail closed to Tier 1 on PacketValidationError. Required packet keys measured 2026-11-06: board_id or id_mapping{board_id,gitreins_task_id}; ch_trace{row,spec,test}; scope.in_scope non-empty and disjoint from out_of_scope; spec_blocks[] and test_refs[] each with id+status(active|current|approved)+digest (test refs also path/selector, path tracked at HEAD). Proof files to create: tests/test_task_context.py (AC-16, exact test name test_scope_and_exclusions_are_explicit) and tests/test_task_packet.py (AC-18/19/20); both absent at base.\n\nSG8 VERIFIED AND MERGED 2026-11-06 (driver tick). Commit 369807b on main (ff-merge; origin parity 0/0). Code: spec judge-packet / judge-handoff assembling the packet the REAL consumer accepts (/home/kara/gitreins engine/auger_packet.py TaskPacketAdapter + engine/judge.py::_prepare_auger_task), from the APPROVED plan so digests survive intake: board_id|id_mapping, ch_trace ids, in/out-of-scope refs, exact test obligations, board acceptance criteria VERBATIM, source digests; validate_judge_packet mirrors the consumer's _unresolved rule set. Proof: tests/test_task_packet.py (7 tests: AC-16 context, AC-18 verbatim/idempotent, AC-19 zero-invocation negative + exactly-one positive, AC-20 false worker summary cannot pass a red obligation) + tests/test_task_context.py (2), all named in the gate pytest arm. Driver-reproduced: evidence/sg8/adapter_probe.py against the real adapter = PROBE RESULT every expectation met (red obligation -> verdict fail citing failed-test-obligation; absent -> exit 4; green -> pass; gitreins tree unchanged); falsifiers.sh 6/6. Gate PASS rc 0 on worktree (585p/2s/914.74s) and mer