 {"status": "pending", "id": "AUG-160", "title": "[P2] GitReins tier1 evidence attaches the NEWEST OLD guard log to every step, so a PASS verdict cites an artifact that says FAIL", "detail": {"fingerprint": "ec3e91233da14dc64f8d1a5cfaf60b1e69887c6cd65ea949e9aadf53c2d6c7c1"}, "priority": "P2", "source": null, "reasoning": "MEASURED 2026-11-08 on verdict cca14d17 (task AUG-158-159-R1, commit 7d4fd96, pass_class=judged, 7/7 items PASS). All three tier1 steps carry data.guard_log=/home/kara/auger/.gitreins/logs/guard-20261105T170854.274025Z.log. That file's header reads run_utc 2026-11-05T17:08:54Z (2.6 days before the verdict's evaluated_at 2026-11-08T07:26:13Z), its own overall line reads 'FAIL (DEGRADED — skipped checks)', and it contains zero ruff output (grep -c ruff -> 0). The newest log in .gitreins/logs/ is still the Nov-5 file, so the task-complete path wrote none; engine/guard_manager.py:1259 newest_guard_log() supplies whatever exists. Net effect: a green verdict's own evidence pointer contradicts it, an auditor cannot tell which run produced the lint/secrets/tests lines, and the same fallback would happily attach an OLD PASS log to a current FAIL step.", "review_notes": null, "ts": null, "acceptance_criteria": "PASS: a fresh verdict's tier1 steps no longer cite a guard log from another run — for every step in `stages.tier1.steps`, `data.guard_log` either is absent or names a file whose `run_utc:` header is within 30 minutes of the verdict's `evaluated_at`. Probe: `cd /home/kara/auger && python3 -c \"import json,pathlib,datetime as dt;d=json.load(open('.gitreins/history/<DATE>/<RUN>/verdict.json'));ev=dt.datetime.fromisoformat(d['evaluated_at']);[print(s['id'], (p:=s['data'].get('guard_log')), (lambda t:(abs((ev-t).total_seconds())<1800 if t else 'absent'))(dt.datetime.fromisoformat([l for l in open(p) if l.startswith('run_utc:')][0].split(':',1)[1].strip().replace('Z','')) ) if p else 'absent') for s in d['stages']['tier1']['steps']]\"` -> every step prints a timestamped path within 1800s, or `absent`.\nPASS: the pre-fix behaviour is reproduced and quoted as the falsifier: `.gitreins/history/2026-11-08/cca14d17/verdict.json` (evaluated_at 2026-11-08T07:26:13Z) attaches `guard_log: /home/kara/auger/.gitreins/logs/guard-20261105T170854.274025Z.log` to ALL THREE tier1 steps (lint, secrets, tests), that file's own header reads `run_utc: 2026-11-05T17:08:54Z` and its `overall:` line reads `FAIL (DEGRADED — skipped checks)`, and no log with a mtime after 2026-11-05T12:08 exists in `.gitreins/logs/` — i.e. three PASS verdict steps point at a 2.6-day-old artifact that says FAIL and contains zero ruff output. Mechanism: the step builders call `newest_guard_log(workdir)` (engine/guard_manager.py:1259) instead of the log of the run producing the verdict, and the `task complete` path writes no log of its own.\nPASS: the fix chooses one of two declared behaviours and the verdict states which — either (a) the `task complete` path writes a per-run guard log so the citation resolves to itself, or (b) the field is omitted entirely when no run-scoped log exists (a MISSING key, never a path to a stranger's log). A path inherited from an unrelated run is not an acceptable third option.\nPASS: a regression test pins it in the gitreins repo (`tests/` file named in that repo's suite): build a tier1 step result while an OLD guard log is present in the logs dir, assert the produced step data does not cite it, and assert the no-log case omits the key. Quote the pytest invocation and its pass count.\nFALSIFIER (pre-fix, run and quote): the probe command in criterion 1 run against cca14d17 prints three steps all resolving to run_utc 2026-11-05T17:08:54Z, 2.6 days before evaluated_at, from a log whose overall line is FAIL.", "complexity": 3, "created_at": "2026-11-08T07:33:49.90834+00:00", "updated_at": "2026-11-08T07:33:49.90834+00:00", "foreman_note": null, "capability_tags": ["gitreins", "evidence", "verdict"], "depends_on": [], "worker_status"