 {"status": "pending", "id": "AUG-161", "title": "The suite is not robust to a relative PATH entry: tests that spawn sys.executable into a scratch cwd die before asserting", "detail": {"fingerprint": "ecbbd8b9a81caf89c7d304fb6e601d39f70482dcaa9cf6fd2d773e55d137a0c5"}, "priority": "P2", "source": null, "reasoning": "Measured 2026-11-09 by the AUG-127 judge (.gitreins/history/2026-11-09/d2447397/verdict.json): with PATH=.venv/bin:$PATH, sys.executable itself is the RELATIVE string '.venv/bin/python3'; tests/test_spec_repository_root.py::run_auger spawns it with cwd set to a scratch consumer repo, so argv[0] resolves against the wrong directory and 6 of 9 tests errored with FileNotFoundError before any assertion ran (anchored: 'assert 1 == 0', '2 failed in 0.19s'). Fixed for that ONE file in 1841d79 (os.path.abspath). Not yet swept: other test files spawn sys.executable too (grep sys.executable tests/*.py = 18 sites) and any site that also sets cwd to a scratch dir has the same latent failure; a green gate never shows it because the gate's PATH is absolute.", "review_notes": null, "ts": null, "acceptance_criteria": "PASS: a written audit enumerates every sys.executable subprocess spawn in tests/ whose call sets cwd=<scratch dir> and shows each is either absolute-resolved or proven unaffected (inherited cwd). PASS: PATH=.venv/bin:$PATH python3 -m pytest -q tests/test_spec_repository_root.py exits 0 with '9 passed' (the fixed instance stays green). PASS: with the audit's fixes applied, PATH=.venv/bin:$PATH python3 -m pytest -q <the audited files> exits 0 and reproduces the absolute-PATH pass count for the same selections.", "complexity": 2, "created_at": "2026-11-09T09:18:30.258149+00:00", "updated_at": "2026-11-09T09:18:30.258149+00:00", "foreman_note": null, "capability_tags": [], "depends_on": [], "worker_status": "pending", "commit_hash": null, "guard_result": null, "ci_result": null, "worktree": null, "branch": null}
 {"status": "complete", "id": "AUG-162", "title": "The live JEV arm reds the whole 15-minute gate on a transient JEV miss: the -1 sentinel is stamped with a real jev_checked_at and the test asserts a numeric verdict", "detail": {"fingerprint": "2ea91887c141e4bdcf547c664d32d162a3b3f0e959691ea62a8138f891111a3e", "evidence": [{"run_id": "6c8f88b2", "ts": "2026-11-10T12:17:32.593159+00:00"}]}, "evidence_run_id": "6c8f88b2", "priority": "P1", "source": null, "reasoning": "Measured 2026-11-10 on ONE unchanged tree (main a0bd6b1, 717-test gate): the live JEV arm tests/test_auger.py::test_feedback_live_proposes_gates_and_asks_a_real_question reds the ENTIRE 15-minute gate whenever the JEV call misses, which makes every GitReins verdict in this repo intermittently unpayable. Evidence: tier1 red in run efd20b1d (05:40:48Z) and again in run e77575d1 (06:31Z) with the identical assertion \"assert q[\\\"jev_checked_at\\\"] and q[\\\"jev_already_answered\\\"] >= 0\" -> \"assert (2026-11-10T06:31:12.560236+00:00 and -1 >= 0)\"; the SAME test passed in-suite on the same tree at 03:03Z (verdict 5c0158a1, 717 passed) and passed ALONE twice at the same head (21.30s, 23.57s). Mechanism: auger.jev() returns (None, \"all N JEV keys failed; last: ...\") on any transport/upstream miss, record_followup() then stamps the documented unknown sentinel jev_already_answered=-1 (auger.py:3389) together with a real jev_checked_at, and the test asserts a NUMERIC verdict (tests/test_auger.py:8321) even though its own docstring says the contract is \"the decision was drilled and the row was stored - never that a model agreed with a plan\". So a third-party hiccup is indistinguishable from a code regression and costs a full 20-minute judge run. Independent lane check this tick: the JEV endpoint answered HTTP 400 to a deliberately malformed probe body (i.e. the keys authenticate and the host is reachable), and one of the 6 discovered OpenRouter keys answers 401 \"User not found\" - a dead key in the rotation adds a failed attempt per call.", "review_notes": null, "ts": null, "acceptance_criteria": "PASS: a question the gate never examined carries NO check stamp: with `auger.recall` forced to return no hits, `feedback --budget 1` stores the follow-up row with `jev_checked_at == \"\"` and `jev_already_answered == -1.0`, spends ZERO JEV calls, and prints the `not gated ... no JEV verdict was produced` line. Falsifier: at 425c846 the same run stamps a real `jev_checked_at` beside `-1` and prints no such line (measured: the new test is RED against HEAD's auger.py, GREEN with the fix). PROOF: cd /home/kara/auger && .venv/bin/python -m pytest -q tests/test_auger.py -k \"no_evidence_could_answer\"\nPASS: a JEV outage stays fail-closed AND is classifiable as a loud skip: with the gate forced to return (None, \"\", \"\", \"all 6 JEV keys failed; last: HTTP 401 User not found\"), `feedback --budget 1` exits 1, stores no follow-up, and prints `WARNING gate unavailable` naming the JEV failure; the live arm's `live_unavailable_reason(out)` returns a skip reason naming JEV+401 for that output and \"\" for an ordinary transcript (so a skip can never mask a real regression). PROOF: cd /home/kara/auger && .venv/bin/python -m pytest -q tests/test_auger.py -k \"jev_unavailable\"\nPASS: the live arm requires the two gate columns to AGREE instead of requiring a model verdict: `tests/test_auger.py::test_feedback_live_proposes_gates_and_asks_a_real_question` asserts `bool(q[\"jev_checked_at\"]) == (q[\"jev_already_answered\"] >= 0)` and still asserts the row exists, is trackable (`opens` edge to D-002), and matches its status branch (satisfies edge or askable). Falsifier: the old `q[\"jev_checked_at\"] and q[\"jev_already_answered\"] >= 0` reds on a healthy tree whenever the gate answers without a model call. PROOF: cd /home/kara/auger && .venv/bin/python -m pytest -q -rs tests/test_auger.py -k \"feedback_live\"\nPASS: the answered path keeps its positive assertion in a DISTINCT test (the fix cannot be \"delete the assertion\"): `test_feedback_turns_a_thin_decision_into_a_named_followup` still requires a numeric noul (0.10) together with a stamped check, and `propagate` no longer writes a sentinel verdict for a question it did not gate. PROOF: cd /home/kara/auger && .venv/bin/python -m pytest -q tests/test_auger.py -k \"feedback or jev or propagate\" (28 passed measured on the fixed tree)\nPASS: the whole gate is green on the MERGED main tree: bash tests/gate.sh with PATH=/home/kara/auger/.venv/bin first, DUCKBRAIN_URL=http://127.0.0.1:3000, DUCKBRAIN_API_KEY from ~/.duckbrain/foreman-status.token and AUGER_GATE_PYTEST_BUDGET=3000s exits 0, so a GitReins verdict in this repo is payable again. PROOF: gate transcript recorded in the goal's evidence (worktree run + post-merge main run)", "complexity": 3, "created_at": "2026-11-10T06:44:11.663752+00:00", "updated_at": "2026-11-10T12:17:32.593159+00:00", "foreman_note": "PREMISE CORRECTED 2026-11-10 (driver): the row's stated mechanism was only half right. Measured in code: feedback stamps g['checked_at'] = now() UNCONDITIONALLY before record_followup (auger.py:3559) and propagate patches jev_checked_at unconditionally (auger.py:2895), so the -1 sentinel lands beside a real timestamp whenever the gate answers WITHOUT a model call — gate_question returns (None,'','',None) on empty recall and on the AUG-063 cosine-miss shortcut. In the two observed reds the CLI printed 'proposed: 1' and exited 0 with a question stored, which cannot happen on the gate_error path (that path exits 1 and stores nothing), so the reds were the NO-CALL path, not a transport outage. Consequence is worse than the flake: propagate skips re-gating any question with jev_checked_at set, so a question nobody gated was never gated again. Fix: stamp only with a verdict (feedback + propagate), keep the JEV-outage path fail-closed with its WARNING, print a distinct 'not gated ... no JEV verdict was produced' line, and let the live arm skip